    "expectedRule": "Chapter 19 scans on every legal move: before the move the scan phase p (0, 1, 2) is compared with the destination phase (x + y) mod 3, a match is scanned, then p advances by one and the move count by one. Before a route is chosen every scanned move exposes the player: exposure +1 and max(1, floor(maxHp x 8%)) damage (no matte_shell or predictive_visor here). Max HP is derived from the build (the decoder recomputes it, so no HP is given as input): 50 + 14 x body 70 + patched_coat 10 = 1040. An exposure therefore costs 83. A refused move does not scan. The first clear of each relay (north, central, south) completes it; completing the third leaves the route pending there and blocks leaving with `三座盲区中继已经闭环，请先选择影路、诱饵或折光路线再离开。`; law/select-panopticon-route works only at the pending relay and fixes the route once. Under the shadow route scanned moves no longer expose. Route nodes open only for the selected route (`完成三座盲区中继后选择影路路线；其余路线将永久关闭。` for shadow_route); the boss edges need three relays and a route (`完成三座盲区中继并选择潜入路线后，万目监察者入口开放。`). Display: title 三相监察律, status `相位:p，移动:m，曝光:e，中继:r/3，路线:<影路|诱饵|折光|未选择>，折光:c/3，诱饵奖励:d/3，Boss快照:<route/exposure/charges|未冻结>`; severity danger before three relays, warning ready for a route, stable ready for the boss, resolved once frozen; meter {relays, 3}. Selecting the boss freezes {route, exposureCount, refractionCharges} (no inverse_prism). Path from panopticon_gate (0,2): watchglass_cache (1,2) target 0 at p0 -> exposed; blindspot_theater (1,1) 2 at p1; blindline_archive (1,0) 1 at p2; north relay (2,0) 2 at p0; upper_entry (3,0) 0 at p1; central relay (3,1) 1 at p2; south relay (3,2) 2 at p0; after choosing shadow, central (3,1) 1 at p1 and south (3,2) 2 at p2 are scanned but hidden, and the boss (4,2) 0 at p0 likewise. The pursuer is a separate run system and is disabled after entry so it cannot ambush the walk. All expected values are frozen here, never read from candidate code."
  },
